@startuml class-vocab
title The vocabulary suite — declared names, generated conversions

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

note as Problem
  **What this exists to remove**

  Hand-written comparisons against spellings,
  scattered across sites that drift apart:
  ""path.is_ident(..)"" against a literal, and a
  ""match ident.to_string().as_str()"" beside it
  listing candidates that no longer matched.

  A declaration generates BOTH the comparison
  and the candidate list, so they cannot
  disagree. And the match becomes exhaustive:
  VERIFIED that adding a name breaks the build
  at every site (E0004) — where an ""is_ident""
  string silently did nothing.
end note

package "proc_macro_flow_traits::vocab" <<Frame>> {

  package "names.rs" <<Rectangle>> {
    class "names!" as Names <<(M,#CFE8CF) macro>> {
      enum + ALL + spelling()
      spellings() + candidates()
      from_spelling() + Display
      From<Self> for &'static str
    }
    class "vocabulary!" as Vocab <<(M,#CFE8CF) macro>> {
      names! + TryFrom<&Ident>
             + TryFrom<&Path>
    }
  }

  package "flags.rs" <<Rectangle>> {
    class "flag!" as Flag <<(M,#CFE8CF) macro>> {
      ZST + TryFrom<&Path>
          + TryFrom<&Meta>
          + FromMeta + ToTokens
    }
  }

  package "values.rs" <<Rectangle>> {
    class "name_value!" as NameValue <<(M,#CFE8CF) macro>> {
      newtype + FromExpr + FromMeta
              + TryFrom<&Expr>
              + TryFrom<&MetaNameValue>
              + Deref + ToTokens
    }
  }

  package "lists.rs" <<Rectangle>> {
    class "meta_list!" as MetaList <<(M,#CFE8CF) macro>> {
      struct + KEYS + FromMeta
             + TryFrom<&Meta>
             + TryFrom<ListBody>
    }
  }

  package "variants.rs" <<Rectangle>> {
    class "variants!" as Variants <<(M,#CFE8CF) macro>> {
      enum + NAMES + FromMeta
           + FromExpr
           + TryFrom<&Meta>
    }
  }

  package "leaves.rs" <<Rectangle>> {
    interface FromExpr {
      +from_expr(&Expr) -> Result<Self>
    }
    interface FromMeta {
      +from_meta(&Meta) -> Result<Self>
    }
    class "leaf!" as Leaf <<(M,#CFE8CF) macro>> {
      FromExpr + FromMeta
      for the Lit family
    }
  }

  package "walk.rs" <<Rectangle>> {
    class Errors {
      -Option<syn::Error>
      --
      +push(Error)
      +absorb<T>(Result<T>) -> Option<T>
      +finish() -> Result<()>
    }
    class "walk_keys / positional" as Walk <<(F,#FFCC88)>> {
      walk_keys(body, candidates, accept)
      positional(body, arity, what)
      last_segment(&Path)
    }
  }
}

Vocab ..> Names : delegates to
Flag ..> FromMeta
NameValue ..> FromExpr
NameValue ..> FromMeta
Leaf ..> FromExpr
Leaf ..> FromMeta
MetaList ..> FromMeta
MetaList ..> Walk : emits a call to
Variants ..> FromMeta
Variants ..> FromExpr
Variants ..> Walk : emits a call to
Walk *-- Errors

note right of FromMeta
  **The uniform field read.**
  ""meta_list!"" reads every field the same way —
  ""<FieldTy as FromMeta>::from_meta(meta)"" —
  whatever shape it is. A flag reads a
  Meta::Path, a leaf the right-hand side of
  ""="", a nested list its own body, and the
  macro neither knows nor cares.

  There is deliberately NO blanket
  ""impl<T: FromExpr> FromMeta for T"": it would
  collide with the specific impls flag! and
  meta_list! generate. Each macro emits its
  own one-liner instead.
  (#leaves/uniform-field-read)
end note

note bottom of FromExpr
  A local trait and not ""TryFrom"", because
  VERIFIED E0117:
  ""impl TryFrom<&Expr> for syn::LitStr"" is a
  foreign trait on a foreign type.

  Newtyping the leaves to get TryFrom back was
  considered and REJECTED — an author's grammar
  names syn's terminals directly, so
  ""Retry { times: LitInt }"" would have become
  ""times: vocab::Int"". FromExpr is what lets
  LitInt stay LitInt.
  (#vocab/orphan-shapes-the-api)
end note

note bottom of Errors
  **Why the walk does not use ""?""**
  VERIFIED: a syn Parse impl using ""?"" over
  three bad elements reports ONE and silently
  drops two. ""syn::Error::combine"" keeps each
  error's own span, so accumulating costs
  nothing and loses nothing.

  The only thing that aborts is a body that
  will not parse as a meta list at all —
  there are no siblings to lose when there
  are no siblings. (#walk/accumulates)
end note

note as Boundary
  **Which macro, and why it matters**

  ""vocabulary!"" — names WE own AND read back out
  of the user's tokens (helper heads, keys).
  Spelling IS identity there.

  ""names!"" — a set that needs a canonical
  spelling for diagnostics but is never matched
  from tokens. ShapeKind is the case.

  ""variants!"" — the ONE place a VALUE is matched
  by name, because the caller needs a value and
  rustc can only check one, never hand one over.
  Documented cost: a renamed import is invisible.

  Never for a selector like
  ""#[shape(AttributeKind::MetaList)]"" — no value
  is needed there, so it is spliced and rustc
  resolves it, import renames and all.
  (#vocab/match-or-splice)
end note

Boundary .. Vocab

note as Typed
  **The walk is typed as of #type-backed.**
  ""ListBody::walk<K: Keys>"" hands the closure the
  resolved VARIANT plus the token that spelled it,
  so a caller's match is exhaustive and every error
  already carries the author's span.

  The string-shaped ""walk_keys"" is DELETED, not
  deprecated — keeping both is how the drift grows
  back. ""const KEYS: &[&str]"" went with it; the
  table is ""Node"", derived from ""Keys"".
  (#keys/one-table)

  A spelling table CANNOT be typed tokens:
  ""Ident::new"" and ""Span::call_site"" are not
  const, so ""const SPELLINGS: &[Ident]"" cannot
  exist. The string survives in exactly one place —
  ""Keys::resolve"" — and allocates nothing, because
  ""Ident: PartialEq<str>"".
  (#keys/table-is-strings-the-rest-is-not)
end note

@enduml
